{{- /*
txref.tmpl is the transaction that paid an order, offered to be copied.

Between "seen" and "confirmed" the shop tells the buyer to wait and the buyer
has nothing to look at; a seller chasing a payment has the same problem from
the other end. This is the one thing either of them can check without asking
the other.

Copied rather than followed. A link that opens a browser from inside a shop's
page is the shop deciding where its reader goes next, and an id pasted into
an explorer is the same answer without that.

Called with the order.
*/ -}}
{{ with .PaymentTx }}
--copy[label=Transaction — press to copy]--
{{ . }}
--/copy--

{{ with explorer }}Paste that into {{ . }} to follow it on the network.
{{ else }}That is the transaction that paid this order.
{{ end }}
{{- end }}
